WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.308
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:03.432 --> 00:00:04.864
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Doors opening.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.666
Second floor.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.267
Departures.

00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:10.741
Check-in and bag drop.

00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:15.756
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:18.056 --> 00:00:21.747
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Excuse me? My suitcase hasn’t arrived.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:24.504
Do you know where I can go to report it?

00:00:24.677 --> 00:00:28.432
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Yes, madam. Lost luggage is that window over there.

00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:32.560
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:34.832 --> 00:00:36.763
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Can you take your boots off, please?

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:37.729
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Sorry?

00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:41.568
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Your boots. Take them off and put them on the belt, please.

00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:45.513
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:51.984
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Boarding for British Airways flight B-A-zero-five-six-four to

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.198
Milan will begin in a few minutes.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:58.867
Passengers in rows fifteen to thirty are invited to board first.

00:00:59.215 --> 00:01:01.815
Please have your passport and boarding pass ready.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.886
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:09.504
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Are you here on vacation?

00:01:09.881 --> 00:01:11.502
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Er, yes, I am.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.202
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> How long are you staying?

00:01:13.695 --> 00:01:14.572
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Two weeks.

00:01:18.094 --> 00:01:18.990
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:01:21.275 --> 00:01:23.240
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Passport and boarding pass, please.

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:26.885
Thanks. How many bags are you checking in?

00:01:30.398 --> 00:01:31.187
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.188
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Hi, darling.

00:01:34.492 --> 00:01:35.956
So good to see you!

00:01:36.104 --> 00:01:37.305
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> You too.

00:01:39.096 --> 00:01:40.207
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> How was your flight?

00:01:40.323 --> 00:01:41.401
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Not too bad.

00:01:41.478 --> 00:01:43.398
Just a fifteen-minute delay.

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:47.054
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

00:01:50.552 --> 00:01:53.743
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Excuse me, are you sure that’s your case?

00:01:53.778 --> 00:01:55.731
It looks exactly like mine.

00:01:56.021 --> 00:01:57.860
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> Well, I think it’s mine.

00:01:58.431 --> 00:01:59.286
Let’s have a look.

00:02:02.475 --> 00:02:05.974
Oh gosh, terribly sorry, it’s not mine.

00:02:07.547 --> 00:02:10.076
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> Look, there’s another similar one coming.

00:02:10.226 --> 00:02:11.954
That’s probably yours.